IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha88-types`

-- Housing Act 1988 (UK) — GOALS 1 AND 2: SECTION 8 AND SECTION 21 NOTICES.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1988-50.txt.

§ `Goals 1 and 2 — notices for possession`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

GIVEN g IS A `Ground kind`, gs IS A LIST OF `Ground kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grounds include` g `in` gs IF
    any (GIVEN h YIELD h EQUALS g) gs

§§ `Goal 1 — section 8 notices`

-- s 8, before the 2025 amendments. (3A) Ground 7A: not earlier than "(a) in
-- the case of a periodic tenancy, the earliest date on which ... the tenancy
-- could be brought to an end by a notice to quit given by the landlord on
-- the same date ...; (b) in the case of a fixed term tenancy, one month
-- after the date on which the notice was served." (4) Ground 14: "not ...
-- earlier than the date of the service of the notice." (4A) Grounds 1, 2,
-- 5-7, 9, 16 (without 7A or 14): "(a) two months from the date of service
-- ...; and (b) if the tenancy is a periodic tenancy, the earliest date" a
-- notice to quit could end it. (4B) "In any other case ... the expiry of the
-- period of two weeks from the date of the service".
@ref s 8(3)(b), (3A), (4), (4A), (4B)
@export The earliest date a notice under s 8 of the Housing Act 1988 (UK) may specify for beginning possession proceedings, in the version before the Renters' Rights Act 2025: for Ground 7A, the earliest notice-to-quit date (periodic) or one month after service (fixed term); for Ground 14, the date of service; for Grounds 1, 2, 5-7, 9 or 16, two months from service or, if later for a periodic tenancy, the earliest notice-to-quit date; otherwise two weeks after service. Refuses for the amended version, whose table of periods is not in the source text. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Section 8 notice`  @desc The version, the date of service, the grounds, the kind of tenancy and the earliest notice-to-quit date
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest date for proceedings under` n MEANS
    CONSIDER n's `version`
    WHEN `as amended by the Renters' Rights Act 2025` THEN
        REFUSE "The s 8(4AA) table of notice periods (Renters' Rights Act 2025 version) is not in the deposited source text."
    WHEN `before the Renters' Rights Act 2025` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the grounds include` `Ground 7A` `in` gs THEN
                IF n's `periodic tenancy` THEN n's `notice to quit could end the tenancy on` ELSE `add months` served 1
            IF `the grounds include` `Ground 14` `in` gs THEN served
            IF `the grounds include` `a ground listed in s 8(4A)` `in` gs THEN
                IF   n's `periodic tenancy`
                THEN `the later of` (`add months` served 2) (n's `notice to quit could end the tenancy on`)
                ELSE `add months` served 2
            OTHERWISE Date (Day served PLUS 14)
    WHERE
        served MEANS n's `served on`
        gs MEANS n's `grounds`

-- s 8(3)(c) "those proceedings will not begin later than twelve months from
-- the date of service of the notice"; (1)(a) proceedings within the notice's
-- time limits.
@ref s 8(1)(a), (3)(c)
@export The last day to begin possession proceedings on a notice under s 8 of the Housing Act 1988 (UK): twelve months from the date of service (the corresponding date). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Section 8 notice`  @desc The date of service
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest date for proceedings under` n MEANS
    `add months` (n's `served on`) 12

@ref s 8(1)(a), (3)
GIVEN n IS A `Section 8 notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date specified is within the limits of` n IF
        n's `date specified for proceedings` AT LEAST `the earliest date for proceedings under` n
    AND n's `date specified for proceedings` AT MOST `the latest date for proceedings under` n

-- s 8(4C)-(4F): a Ground 7A notice must be served within 12 months beginning
-- with the conviction (conditions 1, 3, 5) or the finding (condition 2), or
-- 3 months beginning with the closure order (condition 4) — or with the day
-- any appeal was finally determined, abandoned or withdrawn.
@ref s 8(4C)-(4F)
@export Whether a s 8 notice under the Housing Act 1988 (UK) relying on Ground 7A was served in time (s 8(4C)-(4F)): within 12 months beginning with the conviction or court finding (or the end of an appeal), or 3 months beginning with the closure order (or the end of an appeal). TRUE where Ground 7A is not relied on. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Section 8 notice`  @desc The date of service, the Ground 7A condition and its trigger date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Ground 7A notice was served in time under` n IF
    CONSIDER n's `Ground 7A condition`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST k THEN
        -- "Within the period ... beginning with" the trigger day: not before
        -- it either (added after the independent pass, C4, C20).
        served AT LEAST trigger
        AND CONSIDER k
            WHEN `condition 4 (closure order)` THEN served AT MOST `the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` trigger
            OTHERWISE served AT MOST `the last day of the` 12 `months beginning with` trigger
    WHERE
        served MEANS n's `served on`
        trigger MEANS n's `Ground 7A trigger date`

§§ `Goal 2 — section 21 notices (England)`

-- s 21(4B) "A notice ... may not be given ... (a) in the case of a tenancy
-- which is not a replacement tenancy, within the period of four months
-- beginning with the day on which the tenancy began, and (b) in the case of
-- a replacement tenancy, within the period of four months beginning with the
-- day on which the original tenancy began." (4C): not where the tenancy arose
-- under s 5(2).
@ref s 21(4B)-(4C), (6)-(7)
GIVEN n IS A `Section 21 notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 21 notice was not given too early under` n IF
        n's `arose under s 5(2)`
    OR  n's `given on` GREATER THAN `the last day of the` 4 `months beginning with` (n's `tenancy (or original tenancy) began on`)

-- s 21(1)(b): a fixed term — "not less than two months' notice"; (4)(a)
-- periodic — a date "not earlier than two months after the date the notice
-- was given" (in England, not necessarily the last day of a period:
-- (4ZA)); (4)(b) and not earlier than the notice-to-quit date.
@ref s 21(1)(b), (4)(a)-(b), (4ZA)
GIVEN n IS A `Section 21 notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 21 notice gives enough notice under` n IF
        n's `date specified` AT LEAST `add months` (n's `given on`) 2
    AND (   NOT (n's `periodic tenancy`)
         OR n's `date specified` AT LEAST n's `notice to quit could end the tenancy on`)

@ref s 21(1), (4), (4B)-(4C)
@export Whether a notice under s 21 of the Housing Act 1988 (UK) for a dwelling-house in England is valid as to timing: not given within the first four months of the tenancy (or of the original tenancy, for a replacement tenancy) unless the tenancy arose under s 5(2), and specifying a date at least two months after it was given and, for a periodic tenancy, not before the earliest notice-to-quit date. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Section 21 notice`  @desc The tenancy start, the kind of tenancy, the dates given and specified, and the notice-to-quit date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 21 notice is valid as to timing` n IF
        `the s 21 notice was not given too early under` n
    AND `the s 21 notice gives enough notice under` n

-- s 21(4D) "proceedings ... may not be begun after the end of the period of
-- six months beginning with the date on which the notice was given". (4E):
-- where a periodic notice had to specify a date more than two months after it
-- was given, "after the end of the period of four months beginning with the
-- date specified in the notice."
@ref s 21(4D)-(4E)
@export The last day to begin possession proceedings on a s 21 notice for a dwelling-house in England under the Housing Act 1988 (UK): the end of the six months beginning with the date the notice was given; or, for a periodic tenancy whose notice-to-quit date forced a date more than two months after the notice, the end of the four months beginning with the date specified. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Section 21 notice`  @desc The dates given and specified, the kind of tenancy and the notice-to-quit date
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for s 21 proceedings under` n MEANS
    IF       n's `periodic tenancy`
         AND n's `notice to quit could end the tenancy on` GREATER THAN `add months` (n's `given on`) 2
    THEN `the last day of the` 4 `months beginning with` (n's `date specified`)
    ELSE `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (n's `given on`)
